![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The journal CSV is parsed on every navigation in `evaluateJournalAccess`, even when the raw text is retrieved from the cache. For better performance, especially with larger journals, consider parsing the CSV once when it is fetched and storing the resulting array of entries in the `journalCache`.

```javascript
async function fetchJournalCachedResult(journalUrl) {
  if (!journalUrl) return fetchJournal(journalUrl);

  const now = Date.now();
  if (
    journalCache &&
    journalCache.url === journalUrl &&
    (now - journalCache.fetchedAt) < CACHE_TTL_MS
  ) {
    return {
      ok: true,
      status: journalCache.status,
      text: journalCache.text,
      entries: journalCache.entries,
      error: null,
      fromCache: true
    };
  }

  const result = await fetchJournal(journalUrl);
  if (result.ok) {
    journalCache = {
      url: journalUrl,
      status: result.status,
      text: result.text,
      entries: parseCSV(result.text),
      fetchedAt: now
    };
  }
  return { ...result, entries: journalCache?.entries || [], fromCache: false };
}

async function fetchJournalCached(journalUrl) {
  const result = await fetchJournalCachedResult(journalUrl);
  return result.ok ? (result.entries || result.text) : null;
}
```

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Updating `evaluateJournalAccess` to accept either raw CSV text or a pre-parsed array of entries allows it to benefit from the cached entries suggested in `fetchJournalCachedResult`.

```suggestion
function evaluateJournalAccess(csvOrEntries, keywordsRaw, timeframeMinutes, nowSeconds = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000)) {
  const keywords = Array.isArray(keywordsRaw) ? keywordsRaw : parseLines(keywordsRaw);
  const entries = Array.isArray(csvOrEntries) ? csvOrEntries : (csvOrEntries ? parseCSV(csvOrEntries) : []);
  const match = findRecentKeywordMatch(entries, keywords, timeframeMinutes, nowSeconds);
  return {
    allowed: Boolean(match),
    entries,
    keywords,
    match,
    cutoff: nowSeconds - timeframeMinutes * 60
  };
}
```

_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Fix the remaining-time rounding in `formatExpiry`.**

Using `Math.ceil(seconds / 60)` makes `61` seconds display as `2 minutes left`, and `60` seconds display as `less than 1 minute left`. That makes the diagnostics visibly inaccurate around the boundary.

<details>
<summary>Suggested direction</summary>

```diff
 function formatExpiry(expiresAt) {
   const seconds = Math.max(0, expiresAt - Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000));
-  const minutes = Math.ceil(seconds / 60);
-  if (minutes <= 1) return `${formatDateTime(expiresAt)} (less than 1 minute left)`;
-  return `${formatDateTime(expiresAt)} (${minutes} minutes left)`;
+  if (seconds < 60) return `${formatDateTime(expiresAt)} (less than 1 minute left)`;
+  const minutes = Math.floor(seconds / 60);
+  return `${formatDateTime(expiresAt)} (${minutes} minute${minutes === 1 ? '' : 's'} left)`;
 }
```
</details>

