_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_

**Serialize `chrome.storage.local` updates instead of exposing raw load/save pairs.**

These helpers force every caller into a read-modify-write cycle on shared arrays. If two navigations overlap, the later `set()` can overwrite the earlier mutation and silently drop blocked attempts or intentional sessions. In the session case that also breaks cooldown enforcement, because the first successful unlock may never get persisted.

<details>
<summary>Suggested direction</summary>

```diff
+let blockedAttemptsWrite = Promise.resolve();
+let intentionalSessionsWrite = Promise.resolve();
+
+function updateBlockedAttempts(mutator) {
+  blockedAttemptsWrite = blockedAttemptsWrite.then(async () => {
+    const attempts = await loadBlockedAttempts();
+    mutator(attempts);
+    await saveBlockedAttempts(attempts);
+  });
+  return blockedAttemptsWrite;
+}
+
+function updateIntentionalSessions(mutator) {
+  intentionalSessionsWrite = intentionalSessionsWrite.then(async () => {
+    const sessions = await loadIntentionalSessions();
+    mutator(sessions);
+    await saveIntentionalSessions(sessions);
+  });
+  return intentionalSessionsWrite;
+}
```

Then have `recordBlockedAttempt`, `markAttemptsJournaledLater`, and `recordIntentionalSession` mutate through these queued helpers instead of doing independent load/save calls.
</details>


